# exceeds_evil: S11 and S15 set "evil" as the standard for measuring disgrace, with nothing said about whom the harm falls on. S32 turns "excess of evil" into "a greater evil" for the doer, which is the sense Polus meant in S18 ("suffering wrong was more evil").
# I am unsure whether the text marks this shift clearly enough. It could instead be read as an unstated assumption that the harm counted in the disgrace standard is harm to the agent. If so, every use of the claim is in one sense.
